content:
{
  "findings": [
    {
      "title": "Pregnancy collection window for AMG 510 is inconsistent: 7 days after last dose vs 6 months after last dose of docetaxel, but the text says 'through 7 days after last dose of AMG 510 and 6 months after the last dose of docetaxel' which is correct, but the male partner section says '7 days (AMG 510) or 6 months (docetaxel)' which is consistent. However, the female section says 'through 7 days after last dose of AMG 510' but the male section says 'for an additional 7 days (AMG 510) or 6 months (docetaxel) after discontinuing protocol-required therapies' – this is consistent. No error found here.",
      "page": 149,
      "quote": "through 7 days after last dose of AMG 510 and 6 months after the last dose of docetaxel.",
      "severity": "minor"
    },
    {
      "title": "Lactation collection window is inconsistent: 'through 7 days post final dose' vs 'through 7 days after discontinuing protocol-required therapies' – these are the same, but the first says 'post final dose' and the second says 'after discontinuing protocol-required therapies' – no contradiction.",
      "page": 150,
      "quote": "through 7 days post final dose.",
      "severity": "minor"
    },
    {
      "title": "Pregnancy Notification Form has 'Study Design: Interventional Observational' with checkboxes for Observational, but the study is interventional (AMG 510 and docetaxel), so the form is contradictory.",
      "page": 151,
      "quote": "Study Design: Interventional Observational (If Observational: Prospective Retrospective)",
      "severity": "major"
    },
    {
      "title": "Lactation Notification Form has same contradictory study design field.",
      "page": 152,
      "quote": "Study Design: Interventional Observational (If Observational: Prospective Retrospective)",
      "severity": "major"
    },
    {
      "title": "Pregnancy Notification Form asks for 'Subject age (at onset)' but does not specify onset of what; also, for male subjects, the form has 'Subject Gender: Female Male' but the male partner's information is not captured on the same form; the form is designed for female subjects only, yet the protocol says male subjects' partners' pregnancies are recorded on the same form.",
      "page": 151,
      "quote": "Subject Gender: Female Male",
      "severity": "major"
    },
    {
      "title": "Lactation Notification Form does not have a field for infant gender or mother's age, but the protocol says to collect mother and infant health information; the form has 'Infant gender: Female Male' but no mother's age field.",
      "page": 152,
      "quote": "Infant gender: Female Male",
      "severity": "minor"
    },
    {
      "title": "Hepatotoxicity stopping rules table has inconsistent thresholds: For TBL, temporary withholding is '> 3 x ULN' and permanent discontinuation is '> 2 x ULN at any time' – this is contradictory because permanent discontinuation threshold is lower than temporary withholding threshold.",
      "page": 156,
      "quote": "TBL > 3 x ULN > 2 x ULN at any time",
      "severity": "critical"
    },
    {
      "title": "Hepatotoxicity table: For AST/ALT, temporary withholding includes '> 5 x ULN at any time' and '> 3 x ULN with clinical signs' but permanent discontinuation says 'In the presence of no important alternative causes for elevated AST/ALT and/or TBL values > 3 x ULN (when baseline was < ULN)' – this is not clearly a higher threshold; it's ambiguous.",
      "page": 156,
      "quote": "> 5 x ULN at any time",
      "severity": "major"
    },
    {
      "title": "Hepatotoxicity table: ALP has '> 8 x ULN at any time' for temporary withholding but no permanent discontinuation criterion for ALP, which is inconsistent with the table structure.",
      "page": 156,
      "quote": "ALP > 8 x ULN at any time --",
      "severity": "minor"
    },
    {
      "title": "RECIST v1.1 section says 'subjects should be re-evaluated for response every 6 weeks for the first 48 weeks and then every 9 weeks thereafter' but the protocol's Schedule of Activities (Table 1-1 and Table 1-2) is not provided in this excerpt, so cannot verify consistency; however, the text says 'every 6 weeks' which is typical but not an error per se.",
      "page": 159,
      "quote": "every 6 weeks for the first 48 weeks and then every 9 weeks thereafter",
      "severity": "minor"
    },
    {
      "title": "RECIST v1.1 section says 'measurable lesions are defined as those that can be accurately measured in at least 1 dimension (longest diameter to be recorded) as ≥ 20 mm by chest x-ray, as ≥ 10 mm with CT scan, or ≥ 10 mm with calipers by clinical exam' – this is correct per RECIST 1.1, but the protocol says '≥ 10 mm with calipers' which is not standard; RECIST 1.1 says ≥10 mm with calipers is acceptable, so no error.",
      "page": 160,
      "quote": "≥ 10 mm with calipers by clinical exam",
      "severity": "minor"
    },
    {
      "title": "The protocol references 'Figure 11-2' for Pregnancy and Lactation Notification Forms, but the figure is on page 151 and 152, and the text says 'see Figure 11-2' – that is correct. However, the text says 'see Section 11.4' for SAE reporting, but Section 11.4 is not provided in this excerpt, so cannot verify existence.",
      "page": 149,
      "quote": "reported to Amgen Global Patient Safety as described in Section 11.4",
      "severity": "minor"
    }
  ]
}
